    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, my client has been stuck on their squat for like 3 weeks now. they can't seem to add any weight to the bar even though they're eating enough. how do deload weeks and changing up the volume actually help break a plateau like this?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Deload weeks allow their body to recover and reduce fatigue, which can help improve form and performance when they return to progressive weightlifting. Adjusting volume, such as reducing the number of sets or reps, helps prevent overtraining and can prompt muscle adaptation, which may lead to an increase in strength. A combination of deloading and altering the training volume can facilitate recovery and help your client overcome the plateau.",
